# .cursorrules - Month 1: Visual Architect v2
# Messign Workspace Engineering Spec
# ============================================================

## Project Architecture
- Monorepo: client/ (Vite+React+TS) and server/ (Express.js+TS)
- Database: PostgreSQL with Row-Level Security on 58+ tables
- AI Gateway: LiteLLM centralizes all model calls
- AI Models: Groq (fast categorization), Claude (vision/synthesis)
- Email Builder: Unlayer react-email-editor (v1.x)
- Charts: Recharts
- State: React hooks + custom hooks (useDora, useMarketingApi)
- Testing: Vitest 4.x (client: jsdom + @testing-library/react, server: node)

## Active Module: Marketing
- Layout: client/src/pages/marketing/MarketingLayout.tsx
- All marketing pages under client/src/pages/marketing/
- API client: client/src/lib/marketingApi.ts
- Server routes: server/src/routes/marketing/
- Agent: server/src/agents/marketing/

## Active Work: Visual Architect v2 (Design System)

### Files You Must Read Before Any Task:
- client/src/pages/marketing/lib/designTokens.ts
- client/src/pages/marketing/lib/blockBuilders.ts
- client/src/pages/marketing/lib/designAssembler.ts
- client/src/pages/marketing/lib/emailAiDraftToDesign.ts
- client/src/pages/marketing/components/UnlayerEditor.tsx
- client/src/pages/marketing/components/UnlayerEmailEditor.tsx
- client/src/pages/marketing/components/ContentDetailPanel.tsx
- client/src/pages/marketing/components/cockpit/ContentDetailPanel.tsx
- client/src/pages/marketing/unlayerTemplates/registry.ts
- server/src/agents/marketing/marketingContentStrategistPrompt.ts

### Design Manifest Flow:
1. User requests email content via Dora (chat or Command Center)
2. Content Strategist agent outputs a DesignManifest JSON
3. Client parses manifest, calls assembleDesign()
4. assembleDesign() calls blockBuilders per section
5. Result is valid Unlayer design JSON
6. Unlayer editor.loadDesign() renders it
7. User edits in Unlayer, exports HTML for sending

### Critical Constraints:
- Unlayer design JSON must round-trip: loadDesign -> exportHtml -> works
- All colors from design tokens, never hardcoded hex
- Google Fonts only (no local fonts - Unlayer cant access them)
- Mobile responsive: Unlayer handles stacking, but we must set correct row/column configs
- Email HTML must render in: Gmail, Outlook 2019+, Apple Mail, Yahoo Mail, Outlook.com
- WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1) for all text-on-background combos
- Max email width: 600px (industry standard)
- Preheader text: always include, 100+ chars, hidden from visual

### TypeScript Rules:
- Explicit return types on all exported functions
- No "any" types - use unknown + type guards if needed
- Interface over type alias for object shapes
- Barrel exports from lib/index.ts
- JSDoc on every exported function

### Testing Rules:
- Client tests: Vitest + jsdom + @testing-library/react
- Server tests: Vitest + node environment
- Client test location: client/src/__tests__/ (matching src structure)
- Server test location: server/src/__tests__/ (agents/, dal/, modules/)
- Run client tests: cd client && npm test
- Run server tests: cd server && npm run test:agents
- Every new module must have at least one test file
- Use describe/it/expect (globals: true, no imports needed)

### Naming Conventions:
- Block builders: build[SectionType](content, theme, spacing)
- Token getters: get[TokenType](key)
- Types: PascalCase, prefixed if ambiguous (ManifestSection vs ContentSection)
- Files: camelCase.ts for modules, PascalCase.tsx for React components
- Test files: [module].test.ts matching the source file name
